      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "name": "Strix",
          "informationUri": "https://strix.ai",
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "CWE-200",
              "name": "Unauthenticated information disclosure of internal mesh IP and version via /setup/info",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Unauthenticated information disclosure of internal mesh IP and version via /setup/info"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The `GET /setup/info` endpoint is publicly reachable without authentication and discloses the application's internal mesh listen address (`100.100.108.242:8321`) and software version (`v1.0.10`), aiding reconnaissance and internal-infrastructure mapping."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "The `GET /setup/info` endpoint is publicly reachable without authentication and discloses the application's internal mesh listen address (`100.100.108.242:8321`) and software version (`v1.0.10`), aiding reconnaissance and internal-infrastructure mapping.\n\nAn unauthenticated attacker learns the internal Tailscale/mesh IP:port where the service listens and the exact product version. This reveals internal network topology and the software version, which can be used to target version-specific vulnerabilities. The disclosed address is in the CGNAT range (100.64.0.0/10) and is not directly routable from the public internet, limiting immediate impact to reconnaissance value.\n\nRestrict the `/setup/info` endpoint to only respond before first-boot setup completes, or require authentication once `setup_done` is true. Remove the internal `listen` address from the public response (or omit it entirely once provisioned). Avoid exposing exact software versions publicly, or gate them behind authenticated admin access.",
                "markdown": "The `GET /setup/info` endpoint is publicly reachable without authentication and discloses the application's internal mesh listen address (`100.100.108.242:8321`) and software version (`v1.0.10`), aiding reconnaissance and internal-infrastructure mapping.\n\nAn unauthenticated attacker learns the internal Tailscale/mesh IP:port where the service listens and the exact product version. This reveals internal network topology and the software version, which can be used to target version-specific vulnerabilities. The disclosed address is in the CGNAT range (100.64.0.0/10) and is not directly routable from the public internet, limiting immediate impact to reconnaissance value.\n\nRestrict the `/setup/info` endpoint to only respond before first-boot setup completes, or require authentication once `setup_done` is true. Remove the internal `listen` address from the public response (or omit it entirely once provisioned). Avoid exposing exact software versions publicly, or gate them behind authenticated admin access."
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.3",
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-200",
                  "stride:I"
                ]
              },
              "helpUri": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/200.html"
            },
