      "results": [
        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-200",
          "ruleIndex": 0,
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "Unauthenticated information disclosure of internal mesh IP and version via /setup/info\n\nThe `GET /setup/info` endpoint is publicly reachable without authentication and discloses the application's internal mesh listen address (`100.100.108.242:8321`) and software version (`v1.0.10`), aiding reconnaissance and internal-infrastructure mapping."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "SECURITY.md"
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "/setup/info",
                  "kind": "endpoint"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "primaryLocationLineHash": "c6490bdada31aa2a7c04bbe0a24dd629c439d836649f65dc57a29ffb8624ded9"
          },
          "properties": {
            "security-severity": "5.3",
            "strix_vuln_class_hash": "023c3361500d5224c8144955e8096371e5958726e3993e64887f19aed65823d2",
            "synthetic_location": true,
            "strix": {
              "id": "vuln-0001",
              "severity": "medium",
              "cvss": 5.3,
              "timestamp": "2026-09-22 14:24:57 UTC",
              "target": "https://vault.kervia.ch",
              "endpoint": "/setup/info",
              "method": "GET",
              "cwe": "CWE-200",
              "impact": "An unauthenticated attacker learns the internal Tailscale/mesh IP:port where the service listens and the exact product version. This reveals internal network topology and the software version, which can be used to target version-specific vulnerabilities. The disclosed address is in the CGNAT range (100.64.0.0/10) and is not directly routable from the public internet, limiting immediate impact to reconnaissance value.",
              "technical_analysis": "`GET /setup/info` returns HTTP 200 with a JSON body containing `setup_done`, `listen`, and `version` fields, with no authentication required. This is the first-boot setup status endpoint that remains publicly exposed after provisioning completes (`setup_done:true`). The `listen` field reveals the internal mesh bind address `100.100.108.242:8321` (a Tailscale CGNAT address), and `version` discloses the exact build `v1.0.10`.\n\n```http\nGET /setup/info HTTP/1.1\nHost: vault.kervia.ch\n```\n\n```json\n{\"setup_done\":true,\"listen\":\"100.100.108.242:8321\",\"version\":\"v1.0.10\"}\n```\n\nThe endpoint serves no functional need to unauthenticated internet users after first-boot setup has completed and should not be publicly reachable.",
              "remediation_steps": "Restrict the `/setup/info` endpoint to only respond before first-boot setup completes, or require authentication once `setup_done` is true. Remove the internal `listen` address from the public response (or omit it entirely once provisioned). Avoid exposing exact software versions publicly, or gate them behind authenticated admin access.",
              "counterevidence": "The disclosed IP is a CGNAT/Tailscale address (100.64.0.0/10) that is not directly routable from the public internet, and the version string `v1.0.10` is not itself a secret. No credentials, secrets, or restricted data were returned. This bounds the finding to low/informational reconnaissance value rather than direct unauthorized access.",
              "confidence": "high",
              "severity_change_conditions": "Confirmation that the disclosed mesh address is reachable from an attacker position (e.g. via an already-compromised node or exposed proxy) would raise the severity to medium by turning topology disclosure into a concrete attack path.",
              "poc": {
                "description": "1. Send an unauthenticated `GET` request to `https://vault.kervia.ch/setup/info`.\n2. Observe the HTTP 200 response body discloses the internal listen address and version.",
                "script_available": true
              }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/attack-surface-mapping-endpoint-tech-inventory",
          "ruleIndex": 1,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Attack-surface mapping / endpoint & tech inventory — No issue identified: https://vault.kervia.ch/ (all surfaces)\n\nMapped REST /v1/*, MCP /mcp, admin /admin/*+ /ui/*, and first-boot /setup/* via curl + JS bundle static analysis. Full endpoint inventory recorded in shared note 7d5ec8. Auth model: Bearer (av_ keys) for /v1 + /mcp, session cookie for /admin, public /setup/info. Notable observations (info leak of mesh IP/version via /setup/info, unauthenticated /recovery/recover reaching handler) left for hunting agents."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "https://vault.kervia.ch/ (all surfaces)"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "strix": {
              "coverage_outcome": "no_issue_found",
              "risk_area": "Attack-surface mapping / endpoint & tech inventory",
              "surface": "https://vault.kervia.ch/ (all surfaces)",
              "recorded_by": "Recon & Mapping Specialist",
              "source": "agent_reported"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/authentication-bypass-recovery-flow",
          "ruleIndex": 2,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Authentication bypass / recovery flow — Ruled out: POST /recovery/recover\n\nPOST /recovery/recover reaches handler unauth (invalid_code, not unauthorized) but no auth-bypass or validity oracle found. All string code values (empty/null/missing/any length/case/format) return identical {\"error\":\"invalid_code\"} in ~30ms constant time; non-string code (array/object/number/bool/float) return 400 invalid_request from a JSON type assertion before any code comparison. No state where new_password is accepted without a valid code; empty/null/missing code all → invalid_code. No code-format/length/case/single-use oracle leaks. Method override (X-HTTP-Method-Override/_method) ignored (405/401). Recovery is safe against unauthenticated reset absent a valid code; code entropy/format not enumerable."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "POST /recovery/recover"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "strix": {
              "coverage_outcome": "ruled_out",
              "risk_area": "Authentication bypass / recovery flow",
              "surface": "POST /recovery/recover",
              "recorded_by": "Auth & Recovery Logic Agent",
              "source": "agent_reported"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/rest-api-auth-model",
          "ruleIndex": 3,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "REST API auth model — No issue identified: /v1/* (whoami, secrets)\n\n/v1/whoami and /v1/secrets?vault=<name> both return 401 {\"error\":\"unauthorized\"} without Bearer key. Auth enforced; object-level authz (vault param) untestable without a valid av_ key."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "/v1/* (whoami, secrets)"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
