            "text": "Authentication bypass on REST/MCP gate — Ruled out: /v1/* and /mcp auth bypass (method tampering, header confusion, path/verb case variation)\n\nAuth middleware runs uniformly before handler dispatch. All methods (GET/POST/PUT/PATCH/DELETE/HEAD/OPTIONS) return 401 {\"error\":\"unauthorized\"} on /v1/whoami; /mcp GET/POST 401. Header confusion (Bearer empty/partial/\"av_\" prefix, Basic, X-Api-Key, lowercased scheme, leading spaces, duplicate Authorization headers) all 401. X-Forwarded-For/Real-IP/Host spoofing no effect (401/429). Path case: /V1/whoami and /mcp path variants → 404 (case-sensitive router, not routed to handler), /v1/WHOAMI still 401. No endpoint found that skips the gate."
